senses.gloss:
विदित, अस्, आ, अम्, perceived, known, understood;
apprised, informed; represented; promised, agreed;
(अस्), m. a learned man, sage; (अम्), n. knowledge,
information, representation.

विदल् वि-दल्, cl. 1. P. -दलति, -दलितुम्,
to break or burst asunder, burst or break to pieces;
to be rent or split; to open, expand, blow.

वि-दारण, अम्, n. the act of rending or tearing
asunder, splitting, ripping up, severing, breaking, di-
viding; paining, afflicting; killing, massacre, slaughter;
(अस्, आ), m. f. war, battle; (अस्), m. a tree or rock
in the middle of a stream to which a boat is fastened;
the tree Pterospermum Acerifolium (= कर्णिकार).

विदो वि-दो (see 2. वि-दा), cl. 2. 4. P. -दाति,
-द्यति, -दातुम्, to cut into pieces, cut up, crush;
to destroy.

वि-दधत्, अत्, अती, अत्, distributing, granting, pro-
curing, arranging, prescribing, fixing, performing, &c.;
holding, having, assuming, wearing.
